WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:03.360
(airy music)

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:07.230
- After 9-11, Sikhs become
target of hate crime,

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:10.633
and we felt a need to do
something at that point.

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:14.930
I thought: How can we interact
with other communities,

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:17.040
other people from different faiths

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:18.690
and educate people who Sikhs are?

00:00:19.651 --> 00:00:22.051
We thought, well, let's
start a motorcycle group.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:27.310
- My dad gives people a
point-of-view that is different.

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:30.200
That we aren't bad guys, we are good guys.

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:32.617
(airy music)

00:00:41.269 --> 00:00:42.891
(motorcycle revving)

00:00:42.891 --> 00:00:44.880
- [Narrator] The Sikh Riders
of America are a turban-wearing

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.020
motorcycle group that travels
the country educating people

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.393
about the Sikh religion.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.691
The group was formed
in 2012, after a gunman

00:00:53.691 --> 00:00:54.524
(chanting prayers)

00:00:54.524 --> 00:00:56.724
entered a Sikh temple
and killed six people.

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:00.670
- The estimate is about 250,000 Sikhs living

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:02.490
in the United States.

00:01:02.490 --> 00:01:05.670
There is a large portion
of our American neighbors

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:07.650
who doesn't know who the Sikhs are.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:11.250
Sikh religion believes in equality to all

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.873
and then service to others.

00:01:13.709 --> 00:01:16.150
I have experienced hate, just because

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.211
I'm a Sikh and I look different.

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.200
(motorcycles revving)

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.233
Riding a motorcycle is one
of the big American dream.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:27.300
Sikhs are known warriors in India; we were

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.630
always riding horses,
and so motorcycles are

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:33.240
modern day horses,
that's one of the reasons

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:35.840
we wanted to start, so you
have something in common.

00:01:37.649 --> 00:01:40.430
(inviting music)

00:01:40.430 --> 00:01:42.580
- [Narrator] Each year, The
Sikh Riders of America put

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.343
on fundraisers to raise
money for local charities.

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.760
The fundraisers center
around leading community

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.980
motorcycle rides to local parks, where

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:53.930
in turn, people experience food, dance,

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:55.703
and traditions from Sikh culture.

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.910
And Gurinder is making sure to pass

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.070
his work down to the next generation.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:04.490
- My son has been taking
a part in Sikh Riders

00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:06.920
of America since he was 6 years old.

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.260
He has gone to homeless
shelters to feed the homeless.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.470
I think it would be really
great if I'd be able

00:02:12.470 --> 00:02:14.800
to pass it on to my son.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:17.190
- Seeing my dad do those things makes

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:19.014
me feel proud of my dad.

00:02:19.014 --> 00:02:19.847
(crowd cheering)

00:02:19.847 --> 00:02:23.930
I think what my dad does for
the less fortunate inspires

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:27.610
me to do the same, so
I can follow his lead.

00:02:27.610 --> 00:02:30.030
- It's everyone's event,
you're all a part of us

00:02:30.030 --> 00:02:32.940
because without you, we
haven't been able to do it.

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:33.773
Thank you.

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:39.020
I personally have seen many people after

00:02:39.020 --> 00:02:41.200
they met us, they learn about our religion

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.910
and who we are, they have changed

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:44.453
their view of looking at us.

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:50.130
We have made a big impact on
the communities we live in.

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:53.372
And we have been able to
educate people across America.

00:02:53.372 --> 00:02:55.955
(finale music)

